          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Score points: High (1), Low (1), Jack (1), Game (1). Total 4 points per hand (or more in variants with Joker).',
          gameplay: 'Six cards each. One round of bidding (2 to 4); high bidder names trump and leads. Follow suit; may trump when void (in some variants may trump while holding led suit). Four points per hand: High (ace of trump), Low (deuce of trump), Jack (trick with jack of trumps), Game (side with more card points in tricks: A=4 K=3 Q=2 J=1 10=10). First team to reach target (e.g. 15 or 21) wins.',
          keyRules: [
            'Deal 6 cards each; one round of bidding (2 to 4); high bidder names trump and leads.',
            'Must follow suit when possible; may play trump when void.',
            'Four points per hand: High (ace of trump), Low (deuce of trump), Jack (trick with jack of trumps), Game (more card points in tricks).',
            'Bidding side scores what they made if they make bid; else they lose the bid amount. First to target (e.g. 21) wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "If you have the Ace and King of Trumps, lead the Ace to draw trumps out, then lead the King to let your partner smear a 10 or Jack. If you are defending, try to save your Low (2) for a trick you can win, or smear it on your partner's trick if you think they are winning.",
          intermediate: "The 'Game' Count: Counting the 10s is vital. There are four 10s (40 points). Aces are 4 each (16). Kings are 3 each (12). Queens 2 (8). Jacks 1 (4). Total usually around 80 points. Winning the 'Game' point often decides the match.",
          advanced: "Bidding against the Dealer: The dealer has the last say and can 'steal' the bid for the same amount (in some rules). Bid high enough to force them to 3 or 4.",
          tips: [
            "Don't smear if an opponent might over-trump.",
            'The Jack is worth a game point AND a scoring point.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
