        prompts: {
          human: "Smear (also spelled 'Schmier' or 'Schmear') is a card game played in the northern Midwest of the USA (Minnesota, Wisconsin), closely related to Pitch and High-Low-Jack. It is a trick-taking game typically played with 4 players in partnerships. The objective is to score points for High, Low, Jack, and Game (the 'Smear'), with bids usually starting at 2 or 3. The term 'Smear' also refers to the act of playing a high-point card (like a 10 or Ace) on a partner's winning trick.",
          ai: 'Game: Smear. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
        },
        scoring: {
          description: "High (highest trump in play), Low (lowest trump in playâ€”goes to holder or winner? In Pitch, usually to holder. In Smear, usually to winner of trick? Check rules: In 'Smear', Low often goes to the *capturer* of the low trump, making it distinct from Pitch where it goes to the original holder. Four points per hand: High (player who plays ace of trump), Low (player who plays deuce of trump), Jack (side that wins trick containing jack of trumps), Game (side with more card points in tricks: A=4 K=3 Q=2 J=1 10=10). If bidding side makes at least their bid they score what they made; otherwise they lose the bid amount. First team to reach target (e.g. 15 or 21) wins.",
          winCondition: 'Score points: High (1), Low (1), Jack (1), Game (1). Total 4 points per hand (or more in variants with Joker). First team to reach agreed target score wins.',
